{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139609-trying-to-make-a-custom-mage-2e-setting","id":1139609,"title":"Trying to make a custom Mage 2E setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-11T19:28:58-07:00","id":1139609,"title":"Trying to make a custom Mage 2E setting","content":"Hello! <br /> I've been playing mage for a good long while now, mostly in local live games, but rarely taken the time to run it beyond a couple of one shots (i have run a lot of werewolf and vampire and hunter though). I have a bit of a strange love/hate relationship with the setting so thought i would take the time to sit down and write my own homebrewed setting that felt right, even taking a few bits of inspiration from old WoD mage (paradigm is fun after all!). A nice sandbox city for my players to run around in and explore the themes that are core to the game, from existential reality crisis to the inevitable corruption that theoretical absolute cosmic power brings. Oh and it will be UK setting, gotta run what you know after all!<br /> I decided to write it all up here so i could get some thoughts and opinions from more experienced GMs or just ideas that i can shamelessly steal from casual commentators <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Introducing: Mage - A City of Shattered Dreams<br /> <br /> I have a few base ideas and concepts i want to stick with. <br /> Firstly the players will begin from the very bottom, with the first story arch leading to their awakening, and introduction into the strangeness of the world. <br /> Secondly i dont really want to get too bogged down with the other game lines, i think they have their own themes to explore and at least for now I have no interest is letting them bog down this game too much.<br /> Third. The diamond orders. I want to distance the bottom rung of newly awakened mages (or &quot;tier 1&quot; if you prefer) from the Atlanteans and their ideology and war for the supernal as much possible. I want them to be present in the city as esoteric, elitist, and possibly fanatical small but influencial orders that can easily serve as a potential antagonist as much as a cause of salvation. <br /> The silver ladder are little more then a free masons guild, snobbish, snarky and self righteous, and steeped in ancient ritual and atlantean lore. <br /> The adamantine arrow act like an isolated monestary, constantly training its members with discipline and control, preparing them for a war that seemingly will never come, the war for the Supernal. Think Kun Lun from iron fist, if you can overlook the shows failings. <br /> The guardians of the veil are the most active by far, but are secretive to an even greater extreme then he books suggest, only ever seen in their strange masks, they show up like the boogeymen or the men in black. They dont negotiate and they dont bargain. If someones ranting from the rooftops that they are wizards to everyone with ears, theyll find themselves &quot;removed&quot; before the sun next rises.<br /> The mysterium are no less patronising then their peers, purhaps more so. Then look to get their hands on ever grimoire and supernal relic they can get their hands on. They dont like to share and they dont respect your property. If its magic its theres.<br /> <br /> The free council on the other hand are far larger then all the orders combined but in this setting they are less of an order, and more of a loose alliance of estranged cabals of the modern era, each with its own vastly different philosophy on what magic is and how it is meant to be used. As a result cabals come and go from the council and petty arguements are a plenty, but they all share a disdain for the aloof diamond orders. Its here that the players will encounter most of the friendly NPCs. My goal here is to show a world that reflects most mages that awaken not being in the loop on atlantean secrets beforehand, and as a result they usually tend to turn to the cultural beliefs they are acustomed to to find answers.<br /> One cabal is a university society called YOLOsoc, all about exploring new experiences, highs, lows, and adrenaline rushes. <br /> Another cabal is a facebook group of Nihilist Activists, who organise social outings, along with a group of sleeper friends, that look to subvert and paradoy some aspect of modern society. A lot tend to be into alternative fashion and music.<br /> A cabal formed from a statistical analysis department of the local city council, who formulate equations and probabilities for all many of human behaviour.<br /> Or an Anonymous inspired cabal of cyber criminals and identity thieves, loosely guising their activity as robin hood social justice against the oligarchy.<br /> These are just a few ideas, i need more really, but the free council are where they players will be getting the mojority of their mage NPC interactions.<br /> <br /> As for the seers? I plan to go small with them too, even smaller then the diamond orders. They really are like boogeymen, if only because they can be anyone. The exarchs choose who they speak too, and the voices come, and they only ever get louder and louder until you listen.<br /> In the whole city, its a rare and dangerous event when theres enough of them to fill a cabal, not that they would necessarily know about each other, and many of the commands that are whispered to them in there dreams are nonsensical from their perspective, but the exarchs have a plan, they always have a plan. Trust in your gods.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Ideas? Suggestions? There's a lot i want to fill out yet, i have a few ideas on plots that i might hold close to my chest for now, but ideally i want the players to go out and explore, and find out the difficulty, challenges and consequences of becoming a mage for themselves. The constant temptation to use power for convienience, and the new sensation of seeing the lie for what it is, and the mysteries that invade it, as well as the aggressive agendas of their peers. I want each cabal and order to have its own mysteries and plots and agendas that will sweep the players up when they get too close, with a city full of alternate worlds and strange demenses<br /> <br /> I plan to cut down on jargon a lot too, as i find mage to be way too heavy on the proper nouns in 90% of the games i play, or use alternate jargon depending on whos talking. The free council in particular as i want to make them very much devorced from the diamond and atlantean theory and culture, as though the pentacle was more of a permanant ceasefire then a bonding alliance.<br /> <br /> I havent quite decided how to run the awakening portion of there story or what will bring them together yet, but i want to make sure theres a world to explore first, and besides, i will want to key it to the characters my players make anyway, and i dont have any players yet!<br /> <br /> Is that everything? I think so. I tend to ramble...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6764-nackthepenguin","name":"NackThePenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T19:40:27-07:00","id":1139612,"title":"","content":"So what's the central Mystery of the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T22:58:06-07:00","id":1139642,"title":"","content":"You already seem to be moving towards the idea that the Free Council isn't so much an order as a community of individuals and groups, I would play up that the Diamond Orders may recognize their existence, but doesn't really give them a seat at the secret meetings.<br /> \u200bThe real change I would recommend, and a possible Mystery, would relate to your comment that the Arrow trains constantly for a war that will never happen, I would have it happening right now only in secret. The attitudes you describe for the Arrow, Mysterium and Guardians (everyone but the Ladder really) would make sense if viewed through the lens of a secret war kept hidden even from unaligned Mages.<br /> \u200bThe enemy wouldn't have to be the Seers, at least not directly, it could be Banishers or something totally unrelated to Atlantean theology that threatens the UK.<br /> \u200bIn the beginning the heroes wouldn't have any idea what the Diamond is up to, just that they keep secrets from everyone else, treating them like immature children who should leave real magic to the adults. Then as play continues the heroes catch first hints and then learn about the invisible war taking place in their city.<br /> \u200bThen they find themselves wondering which side they should support, if either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T06:00:43-07:00","id":1139689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139609-trying-to-make-a-custom-mage-2e-setting?p=1139612#post1139612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the central Mystery of the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this, you need a reason that Mages are there in the first place, and to consider how it's affecting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}